{
	title: 'Quiet navigation commands and one-card command output',
	spec: 'A human-typed command whose effect the tabs or session status already show records nothing on success: /go, /move, /unread, /new, /close, /resume and /pause (the Paused. card that Esc also writes is its record). A failure, or any reply that says something, records the command and its output as usual. A key or tab drag that runs one of these must also record nothing. The command still answers a model tool call with its result, and commands that the model or another session runs stay recorded. Every other typed command is one card in terminal and web: its header is the time and the command text, and its body is what it said; a command that says nothing is one row (time, command). Synthetic text, prompt-file changes and commits keep their own cards. History keeps command and output records unchanged; clients join them, live and restored alike. Output text does not repeat the command name (/rename says Old → New).',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'SlashCommand.quiet marks a command; host/slash.ts command() runs a quiet human command first and records it (typed + report) only if its reply has keys other than result. Confirmations moved from say to result so the model tool call still gets them.',
		'A quiet command leaves no command record, so host.submitted cannot detect a resend with the same client id: a client that crashes between submit and ack may run /new twice. Accepted: the ack follows at once, and the other quiet commands are idempotent.',
		'Joining lives in common/transcript.ts (joins, join, joined) for fold and fromSnapshot alike; the joined item is a command with output and error. titles.author heads it by its text; a command with no output has no header and draws as one stamped row.'
	],
	needs: ['et'],
	foldInto: ['et']
}
